    "updated_at": "2026-09-09T13:12:06Z",
    "body": "I have the same problem. It's only a problem for the PocketID OIDC provider. I create a group with the same name as an external user. I add a local user to the group and grant the group permission to view the board. However, after clicking \"**Save group permissions,**\" the settings reset, and the group **is not added to the viewing list**.\nThe `homarr-admins` group is configured with administrator privileges, and everything works for that group. However, I cannot make every user an administrator.\n\n`services:\n  homarr:\n    container_name: homarr\n    image: ghcr.io/homarr-labs/homarr:latest\n    restart: unless-stopped\n    volumes:\n      - /opt/projects/homarr/configs:/app/data/configs\n      - /opt/projects/homarr/icons:/app/public/icons\n      - /opt/projects/homarr/data:/appdata\n      - /opt/projects/homarr/backgrounds:/app/public/imgs/backgrounds\n    environment:\n      - TZ=Asia/Almaty\n      - SECRET_ENCRYPTION_KEY=80b45b446bc7dbe542699f71c969dfd2f74c33b863f30173f14e0ff7aedf1910\n      - DISABLE_UPGRADE_MODAL=true\n      - AUTH_PROVIDERS=credentials,oidc \n      - AUTH_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=${OIDC_CLIENT_ID}\n      - AUTH_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=${OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET}\n      - AUTH_OIDC_ISSUER=https://${AUTH_DOMAIN}/\n      - AUTH_OIDC_CLIENT_NAME=PocketID\n      - AUTH_OIDC_SCOPE_OVERWRITE=openid email profile groups\n      - AUTH_OIDC_GROUPS_ATTRIBUTE=groups\n      - AUTH_OIDC_AUTO_LOGIN=false\n    networks:\n      nginx_proxy:\n        \nnetworks:\n  nginx_proxy:\n    external: true\n`\n\nv1.77.0",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
